From: Husarion <support@husarion.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Host: FASTDDS_HOST_ID fixes the host id that SHM locators carry

Host::Host() computes the host id once per process, as an MD5 fold of the IPv4
addresses IPFinder::getIP4Address() returns (interfaces with IFF_RUNNING, the
loopback excluded). Every SHM locator carries it (SHMLocator::create_locator()
writes it into address[1..2]), and ProxyDataFilters drops a remote SHM locator
whose id differs from this process's (SHMLocator::is_shm_and_from_this_host()).
The same id is bytes 2..3 of every GUID prefix (GuidUtils, through
SystemInfo::host_id()), which is_from_this_host() and PDPSimple's same-host test
compare. So the id is a property of the moment a process starts, not of the
host: on a robot whose Ethernet gets carrier or a DHCP address during boot,
processes started before and after the change compute different ids, and an
SHM-only world splits into islands that never see each other's locators.
Reproduced on a Panther/Lynx: add an IPv4 address to eth0 and restart one
container, it sees only itself; remove it and restart, it sees all 28 nodes;
the same with eth0 down when the container starts.

When FASTDDS_HOST_ID is set and parses with strtoul(base 0) as 0 to 0xFFFF,
that value is the host id; unset, empty or unparsable (a warning), the id is the
address hash as before. Opt in only, with no default value: a fixed default
would make SHM+UDP participants on two different hosts accept each other's SHM
locators, so a deployment sets one value per host for every process that shares
its /dev/shm. Host::instance() is the only source of the id for SHM locators
and GUID prefixes; the one other computation, RTPSDomain::createParticipant()'s
hash of the addresses plus metatraffic_external_unicast_locators, only renames
the GUID prefix of a participant configured with external locators and does not
touch SHM locators, so it keeps its upstream behaviour. Private header only, no
ABI or wire change: without the variable a patched process computes exactly
the id a stock one computes.

---
--- a/src/cpp/utils/Host.hpp
+++ b/src/cpp/utils/Host.hpp
@@ -15,6 +15,9 @@
 #ifndef UTILS_HOST_HPP_
 #define UTILS_HOST_HPP_
 
+#include <cerrno>
+#include <cstdlib>
+
 #include <fastdds/rtps/common/Locator.h>
 
 #include <fastrtps/utils/md5.h>
@@ -98,10 +101,13 @@ private:
 
     Host()
     {
-        // Compute the host id
-        fastdds::rtps::LocatorList loc;
-        fastrtps::rtps::IPFinder::getIP4Address(&loc);
-        id_ = compute_id(loc);
+        // Compute the host id, unless FASTDDS_HOST_ID fixes it
+        if (!id_from_environment(id_))
+        {
+            fastdds::rtps::LocatorList loc;
+            fastrtps::rtps::IPFinder::getIP4Address(&loc);
+            id_ = compute_id(loc);
+        }
 
         // Compute the MAC id
         std::vector<fastrtps::rtps::IPFinder::info_MAC> macs;
@@ -134,6 +140,31 @@ private:
         }
     }
 
+    // FASTDDS_HOST_ID (decimal, 0x hex or 0 octal, 0 to 0xFFFF) replaces the
+    // address hash, so processes started before and after an interface change
+    // agree on the host id. Unset or unparsable: the address hash, as before.
+    static bool id_from_environment(
+            uint16_t& id)
+    {
+        const char* value = std::getenv("FASTDDS_HOST_ID");
+        if (nullptr == value || '\0' == value[0])
+        {
+            return false;
+        }
+        char* end = nullptr;
+        errno = 0;
+        unsigned long parsed = std::strtoul(value, &end, 0);
+        if (0 != errno || end == value || '\0' != *end || '-' == value[0] || parsed > 0xFFFFUL)
+        {
+            EPROSIMA_LOG_WARNING(UTILS, "Ignoring FASTDDS_HOST_ID '" << value <<
+                    "' (not 0 to 0xFFFF), the host id comes from the IPv4 addresses");
+            return false;
+        }
+        id = static_cast<uint16_t>(parsed);
+        EPROSIMA_LOG_INFO(UTILS, "Host id " << id << " from FASTDDS_HOST_ID");
+        return true;
+    }
+
     uint16_t id_;
     uint48 mac_id_;
 };
